  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Business Plan Competition Implementation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is one component of the wider Harnessing the Demographic Dividend programme led by the Secretariat of State for Youth and Employment (SEJE) and the World Bank. The BPC aims to stimulate employment, address market failures that constrain the creation and growth of youth businesses. It will design and implement a nationwide business plan competition for young people aged 18-35 yrs with a focus on female entrepreneurs and start-ups. KPMG Mozambique is the lead organisation with Plan Mozambique and Plan UK as subs. The main focus is Youth and Women&apos;s Economic Empowerment. The BPC has two phases: 1. Pilot Phase: covering the Province and City of Maputo;  around 1,000 applications will be received and 350 candidates will be selected. These will be trained on the preparation of business plans for subsequent submission.  Of these, 50 winning projects will be selected and financed. 2. National Phase: a nationwide campaign will be launched for young people across the country. At this stage 10,000 applications will be received and selected. Up to 3,500 will be selected for trained to further refine and develop their plans. 500 business plans will then be selected for funding. The total contract value is $900,000 of which Plan&apos;s original value is $422,381. Plan&apos;s role is on Environmental and Social Safeguards and Gender Inclusion.</narrative>
  </description>
